(195,60,'ions for test-time adaptation.\nMethods for 3D segmentation, like those for 2D dense pre-\ndiction tasks, primarily rely on model adaptation techniques.\nThese include approaches using 3D reconstruction [253]\nor pseudo-labeling [268], [400] at test time. Some methods\n\n18\nTable 5:Test-time adaptation applications.This table summarizes representative test-time adaptation methods according to\nwhat they adapt (Section) and their main applications (Section) revealing the emerging research opportunity of test-time\nadaptation beyond model adaptation and image classification (Section).\nImage-level Video-level 3D-level Beyond-vision\nClassification Dense Enhance Classification Dense Enhance Classification Dense RL NLP Multimodal\nModel adaptation\nAuxiliary self-supervision [202], [293] [246] [40], [263] - [22], [199] [41], [351] [220] [253], [332] [197], [283] [16], [102]\nEntropy minimization [319], [375] [170], [281] - [356] - - - - - - [196], [334]\nPseudo-labeling [95], [134] [132], [313] - [185], [342] - - - [268], [278] - - [65], [303]\nFeature alignment [222], [285] [118] [53] [188], [227] [12], [272] - - - - - -\nInference adaptation\nBatch-wise inference [131], [379] - - - - - [327] - - [310] -\nSample-wise inference [294], [341] [326], [355] - - - - - - - - -\nNormalization adaptation\nTarget statistics [90], [376] - - - - - - - - - -\nStatistics combination [186], [271] [148], [401] [353] - - - - - - - -\nStatistics inference [61], [138] - - - - - - - - - -\nSample adaptation\nFeature adjustment [243], [340] - - - - - - - - - [2]\nInput adjustment [83] - - - - - - - - - -\nPrompt adaptation\nText-prompting [219], [261] [66] - - - - - - - - [213], [378]\nEmbedding-prompting [290], [302] - [39] - - - - - - - [269], [279]\nachieve 3D segmentation with both image and point cloud\nmodalities [29], [30], [278], [332].\nOther applications.Recently, test-time adaptation ap-\nproaches have also been investigated in other 3D-level\napplications. For 3D pose