(44,NULL,NULL,13,35,'Write a code about Need to get plot accuracy with relevant to training and testing uk dale dataset in nilmtk using google colab platform. guild me with codes, in ','{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-9PCyLCxPeWjKLqR3HfLC2MIhyEi2A\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1715795093,\"model\":\"gpt-3.5-turbo-0125\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Sure, here is the code to train and test a NILMTK model on the uk dale dataset in Google Colab:\\n\\n```python\\n!pip install nilmtk\\nimport nilmtk\\n\\nfrom nilmtk import DataSet\\nfrom nilmtk.utils import print_dict\\n\\n# Load the UK Dale dataset\\nuk_dale = DataSet(\'data\\/UKDALE.h5\')\\n\\n# Train the model on training data\\ntrain = uk_dale.buildings[1].elec\\ntrain.set_window(start=\'2013-04-12\', end=\'2013-04-13\')\\ntrain.selected_cols = [2]  # Just using one appliance for simplicity\\n\\n# Test the model on testing data\\ntest = uk_dale.buildings[1].elec\\ntest.set_window(start=\'2013-04-13\', end=\'2013-04-14\')\\ntest.selected_cols = [2]  # Just using one appliance for simplicity\\n\\nfrom nilmtk import API\\n\\n# Train the model\\napi = API(train)\\napi.train()\\n\\n# Test the model\\npredicted_power = api.disaggregate(test)\\n\\nfrom sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\\n\\n# Calculate accuracy\\naccuracy = accuracy_score(test.power_series_all_data(), predicted_power)\\nprint(f\\\"Accuracy: {accuracy}\\\")\\n```\\n\\nThis code loads the UK Dale dataset, trains a NILMTK model on a specific appliance, and then tests the model on another day. Finally, the accuracy of the model is calculated using the `accuracy_score` function from scikit-learn. You can run this code in Google Colab to get the accuracy of the model for the UK Dale dataset.\"},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":43,\"completion_tokens\":333,\"total_tokens\":376}}','Sure, here is the code to train and test a NILMTK model on the uk dale dataset in Google Colab:\n\n```python\n!pip install nilmtk\nimport nilmtk\n\nfrom nilmtk import DataSet\nfrom nilmtk.utils import print_dict\n\n# Load the UK Dale dataset\nuk_dale = DataSet(\'data/UKDALE.h5\')\n\n# Train the model on training data\ntrain = uk_dale.buildings[1].elec\ntrain.set_window(start=\'2013-04-12\', end=\'2013-04-13\')\ntrain.selected_cols = [2]  # Just using one appliance for simplicity\n\n# Test the model on testing data\ntest = uk_dale.buildings[1].elec\ntest.set_window(start=\'2013-04-13\', end=\'2013-04-14\')\ntest.selected_cols = [2]  # Just using one appliance for simplicity\n\nfrom nilmtk import API\n\n# Train the model\napi = API(train)\napi.train()\n\n# Test the model\npredicted_power = api.disaggregate(test)\n\nfrom sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n\n# Calculate accuracy\naccuracy = accuracy_score(test.power_series_all_data(), predicted_power)\nprint(f\"Accuracy: {accuracy}\")\n```\n\nThis code loads the UK Dale dataset, trains a NILMTK model on a specific appliance, and then tests the model on another day. Finally, the accuracy of the model is calculated using the `accuracy_score` function from scikit-learn. You can run this code in Google Colab to get the accuracy of the model for the UK Dale dataset.','JT4YkIjW3D14NQk6vboAkny4RryHhflp7NnaRm23YFUXftuWRRrUJ4c2TRqC8R2dnVVJkT2GPwjM1f9JehtFfxd3MyjS3rodnjthth9Zzgfljvm2C98WcPOKedaSEiwUHozhg5N6ORJHFN6LKffw99uNFBsqYqxXBq2rwU0qBiYjFPce62sCfP5ly9Y9QfCpF9r9Tj5VJqbX4nz3CaA7Ti1Xb0FgDzjTnzz6kbOa9wVS79vkoyzppwNWcqyaVPE9','214','0','2024-05-15 17:45:00','2024-05-15 17:45:00','New Workbook','M9NTgQopramod-dilshan-workbook',NULL,NULL,NULL,'COMPLETED'),
