re is a code snippet that can help you load the UK Dale dataset and plot the accuracy with relevance to training and testing:\n\n```python\n!pip install nilmtk\n\nfrom nilmtk import DataSet\n\n# Load the UK Dale dataset\nuk_dale = DataSet(\'data/UKDALE.h5\')\n\n# Get the training and testing data\ntrain = uk_dale.buildings[1].elec\ntest = uk_dale.buildings[2].elec\n\n# Train a model\nfrom nilmtk import API\n\napi = API()\napi.train(train)\n\n# Test the model\ntest_mains = test.mains().all_meters()[0]\ndisag = api.disaggregate_chunk(test_mains)\n\n# Calculate accuracy\naccuracy = disag.accuracy()\n\n# Plot the accuracy\ndisag.plot()\n\nprint(\"Accuracy:\", accuracy)\n```\n\nMake sure to replace \'data/UKDALE.h5\' with the correct path to your UK Dale dataset file.\n\nLet me know if you encounter any issues with this code!','hjsAouulKmiHDhHEvUOaMxOJrUjCPlR28PPMW9QowzZaetzAaABIJOXU5L3QcEdkzYxYjxtNxk8liYRJNeLSULR4ec8um7dKFenZTqJzDDTSr4AqRYfNqhnYnrgpfXu4MenPO4ZjNpHGAFD5kNzMFA9kCoGusANRWSYB8IlT82DtRSTggjxRZT9tegetfnq4CcyZW1hUiKTRSmYQtBpmACDuWy56oAiKZtREiD2CG23yr5ALJnSpiJextMdub3J3','158','0','2024-05-15 17:52:15','2024-05-15 17:52:15','New Workbook','0O8Hp6dpramod-dilshan-workbook',NULL,NULL,NULL,'COMPLETED'),
