(78,NULL,NULL,40,35,'Write a code about terabox api \r\nhttps://jolly-union-9cc3.shraj.workers.dev/?id={video id}\r\nhis response \r\nWrite tg terabox video dwnler bot\r\n#EXTM3U\r\n#EXT-X-TARGETDURATION:15\r\n#EXT-X-DISCONTINUITY\r\n#EXTINF:2,\r\nhttps://crimson-feather-f1eb.shraj.workers.dev/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fv1.freeterabox.com%2Fvideo%2Fnetdisk-videotran, in Python','{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-ATNwhDlULvY9UHxQTgIijvlXQJs40\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1731566923,\"model\":\"gpt-3.5-turbo-16k-0613\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"To download a video using the Terabox API in Python, you can use the following code:\\n\\n```python\\nimport requests\\n\\nvideo_id = \\\"your_video_id\\\"\\n\\n# API endpoint URL\\nurl = f\\\"https:\\/\\/jolly-union-9cc3.shraj.workers.dev\\/?id={video_id}\\\"\\n\\n# Send GET request to the API\\nresponse = requests.get(url)\\n\\n# Check if the request was successful\\nif response.status_code == 200:\\n    response_text = response.text\\n    \\n    # Extract the video URL from the response\\n    start_index = response_text.find(\\\"https:\\/\\/crimson-feather-f1eb.shraj.workers.dev\\/?url=\\\")\\n    end_index = response_text.find(\\\".m3u8\\\") + len(\\\".m3u8\\\")\\n    video_url = response_text[start_index:end_index]\\n    \\n    # Download the video\\n    video_response = requests.get(video_url)\\n    \\n    # Save the video to a file\\n    with open(\\\"downloaded_video.mp4\\\", \\\"wb\\\") as video_file:\\n        video_file.write(video_response.content)\\n        \\n        print(\\\"Video download complete!\\\")\\nelse:\\n    print(\\\"Error occurred while accessing the API.\\\")\\n```\\n\\nMake sure to replace \\\"your_video_id\\\" with the actual video ID you want to download. The code sends a GET request to the Terabox API, extracts the video URL from the response, and then downloads the video using the extracted URL. The downloaded video will be saved as \\\"downloaded_video.mp4\\\" in the same directory as the Python script.\"},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":128,\"completion_tokens\":312,\"total_tokens\":440}}','To download a video using the Terabox API in Python, you can use the following code:\n\n```python\nimport requests\n\nvideo_id = \"your_video_id\"\n\n# API endpoint URL\nurl = f\"https://jolly-union-9cc3.shraj.workers.dev/?id={video_id}\"\n\n# Send GET request to the API\nresponse = requests.get(url)\n\n# Check if the request was successful\nif response.status_code == 200:\n    response_text = response.text\n    \n    # Extract the video URL from the response\n    start_index = response_text.find(\"https://crimson-feather-f1eb.shraj.workers.dev/?url=\")\n    end_index = response_text.find(\".m3u8\") + len(\".m3u8\")\n    video_url = response_text[start_index:end_index]\n    \n    # Download the video\n    video_response = requests.get(video_url)\n    \n    # Save the video to a file\n    with open(\"downloaded_video.mp4\", \"wb\") as video_file:\n        video_file.write(video_response.content)\n        \n        print(\"Video download complete!\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Error occurred while accessing the API.\")\n```\n\nMake sure to replace \"your_video_id\" with the actual video ID you want to download. The code sends a GET request to the Terabox API, extracts the video URL from the response, and then downloads the video using the extracted URL. The downloaded video will be saved as \"downloaded_video.mp4\" in the same directory as the Python script.','kQQF5rdoTSXqfqq7xuJPW44oiPI7IXLlFvR6O5YLFcZI6MT3ZHmL4NH9Icbr08qP77OfBOjy4yVG70LJmqpiVrfzeJCeBvgVZeoS8aSUIi7IE8STSizQ9uRx9I40N8oF1XXkaYtF0tNQpB5urIED5f1yJF8KPo9lfPv9GVC42cNf3hmtunKPgFO7UIAlLlD3dbKRb63MtnnHovKIdFr0b1uvFKyxA09GLVaagEvOWUO8kZJxBGGIrR9ts57UbrnY','201','0','2024-11-14 06:48:46','2024-11-14 06:48:46','New Workbook','AXAAKvLdeepak-kushwah-workbook',NULL,NULL,NULL,'COMPLETED'),
