(7,5,2,'I want to improve my English skills','That\'s great to hear! Improving your English skills can open up many opportunities for you. Here are some tips to help you improve:\n\n1. Practice speaking and listening: Try to have conversations in English with native speakers or practice speaking by yourself. You can also watch English movies, listen to English music, or follow English podcasts to improve your listening skills.\n\n2. Reading and writing: Read English books, newspapers, articles, or any English material that interests you. Additionally, try to write in English regularly, whether it\'s journaling, emailing, or blogging.\n\n3. Grammar and vocabulary: Work on grammar rules and learn new vocabulary words. There are many online resources, textbooks, and apps available to help you with this.\n\n4. Take English classes: Consider enrolling in an English course or finding a tutor to give you structured learning and feedback.\n\n5. Practice regularly: Consistency is key when improving any skill, including language learning. Set aside time each day to practice your English skills.\n\nRemember, the key to improvement is consistent practice and exposure to the language. Good luck in your English learning journey! If you have any specific questions or need assistance, feel free to ask.','That\'s great to hear! Improving your English skills can open up many opportunities for you. Here are some tips to help you improve:<br/><br/>1. Practice speaking and listening: Try to have conversations in English with native speakers or practice speaking by yourself. You can also watch English movies, listen to English music, or follow English podcasts to improve your listening skills.<br/><br/>2. Reading and writing: Read English books, newspapers, articles, or any English material that interests you. Additionally, try to write in English regularly, whether it\'s journaling, emailing, or blogging.<br/><br/>3. Grammar and vocabulary: Work on grammar rules and learn new vocabulary words. There are many online resources, textbooks, and apps available to help you with this.<br/><br/>4. Take English classes: Consider enrolling in an English course or finding a tutor to give you structured learning and feedback.<br/><br/>5. Practice regularly: Consistency is key when improving any skill, including language learning. Set aside time each day to practice your English skills.<br/><br/>Remember, the key to improvement is consistent practice and exposure to the language. Good luck in your English learning journey! If you have any specific questions or need assistance, feel free to ask.','LHtj2yFtNfr76L3EsNOlUFU8rbmWN0fBEXEnRBRRcB95RJhG4ual2J7FaQi3IJMKFRfRquaa8GqieJN8rJHm8LI4ZIpsIXfAAXyjBeas2xclA7VX4vao7pkE1hZ0gvRqKy7S6SgYmDKml1VxybzTE4wsjYadCLoyGzigjhveEbds2TThoRH7cpNH9oBaAgwxnQpRbfJcn8DsW2HYtY9JRELHt65u6Pj7Fzm6VaHMI7wsocYaYtpGnLAROYnm4LrS','195','0','2024-03-20 01:15:43','2024-03-20 01:15:48','',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0),
