(116,61,72,'Can you copyright dance monkey song in germany','I am not a copyright lawyer, but I can provide some general information. In Germany, musical works such as songs can be protected under copyright law. However, copyright protection is automatically granted to the creator as soon as the work is created, without the need for official registration or filing. This means that the song \"Dance Monkey\" is likely already protected under copyright in Germany, as it is an internationally popular song.\n\nIf you are the creator of the song and want to enforce your copyright, you may consider marking your work with the copyright symbol (©), your name, and the year of creation to provide notice of your copyright claim.\n\nIf you have specific legal questions or require official advice, I recommend consulting with a copyright lawyer or a legal professional familiar with the copyright laws in Germany.','I am not a copyright lawyer, but I can provide some general information. In Germany, musical works such as songs can be protected under copyright law. However, copyright protection is automatically granted to the creator as soon as the work is created, without the need for official registration or filing. This means that the song \"Dance Monkey\" is likely already protected under copyright in Germany, as it is an internationally popular song.<br/><br/>If you are the creator of the song and want to enforce your copyright, you may consider marking your work with the copyright symbol (©), your name, and the year of creation to provide notice of your copyright claim.<br/><br/>If you have specific legal questions or require official advice, I recommend consulting with a copyright lawyer or a legal professional familiar with the copyright laws in Germany.','ThT5cjhs3WbpKwVml9sxlVuyj3Vavci7x020gMQ7MRLdLBW2kcKszZarhLr4IUO1A7Wj9TvqfyJpjOBhDiqpo90x5BF6k1yxc9uyZU0wKf9tMmmdOoZwjEnABUP51G5T6pvOMkXyMHWHZA6GnTVVVxRHFrIDvEWxBT4NkZ5D2Dof1RpHefaNryruDFxwjhbKKgwqUvSK1mMcxPPfculfyi2lcsXRiK6